  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">A Comprehensive Response to Prevent and Combat Trafficking in Persons in the Solomon Islands</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The American Bar Association Fund for Justice and Education (ABA), with J/TIP&apos;s support, has been operating in the Solomon Islands since 2010. ABA works with civil society, government, and law enforcement to generate a comprehensive response to prevent trafficking in persons (TIP), and to strengthen efforts to protect survivors and prosecute violators. The goal of the project is to reduce the prevalence of trafficking in the Solomon Islands and to develop an effective, coordinated response to the problem. To this end, the program has four objectives: 1.) strengthen data collection among legal service providers and law enforcement for reporting, referrals, and prosecution; 2.) build awareness of TIP among vulnerable communities, government, and legal service providers; 3.) enhance legal services and counseling for trafficking survivors; and 4.) strengthen regional sharing of information.</narrative>
  </description>
